            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kim"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These are nice cookies; easy to make and really do keep their shape after being baked. My only caveat is that they simply don't have the flavor that a butter cookie does; and that's, of course, due using shortening instead. I only made a half batch of these, and got about 20 cookies of various sizes. I also had found the dough to be very workable; and had no issues rolling it out. I frosted the cookies with Glossy Royal Icing from this site. Thanks for the recipe!",
